@TITLE The Odyssey
@AUTHOR After Homer
@START troy_aftermath
@DESC_TEXT Epic voyage home from the fall of Troy.

@ROOM troy_aftermath
@DESC
The great city of Troy
smolders behind you. Ten
years of war are ended.
Your crew cheers upon the
black ships. Ithaca and
Penelope await far away.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Set sail for home" -> open_sea
@CHOICE "Raid the coast" -> raid_coast

@ROOM raid_coast
@DESC
Greed seizes you. Your men
plunder a coastal town,
gorging on wine and gold.
But dawn brings soldiers.
You barely escape. Dark
clouds gather overhead.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET gods_angry
@CHOICE "Flee to the ships" -> open_sea

@ROOM open_sea
@DESC
The wine-dark sea spreads
before your twelve ships.
Fair winds carry you west.
@IF gods_angry
Yet the sky grows black.
Poseidon stirs the deep.
@ENDIF
A storm descends without
warning. For nine days you
are driven off course.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Ride out the storm" -> lotus_island

@ROOM lotus_island
@DESC
You beach on a strange and
drowsy shore. Sweet scent
hangs heavy in the air.
Smiling natives approach,
offering blossoms of
unearthly beauty.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Eat the lotus" -> lotus_doom
@CHOICE "Refuse the fruit" -> lotus_rescue
@CHOICE "Explore the shore" -> lotus_crew

@ROOM lotus_doom
@DESC
The blossom melts on your
tongue like honey and
starlight. A warm fog
fills your mind. Who is
Penelope? Where is Ithaca?
You no longer care.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You forgot home, wife, and name. The lotus claimed you."

@ROOM lotus_crew
@DESC
Deeper inland, you find
your scouts sprawled among
flowers. Their eyes are
glazed. They smile but do
not know you. The lotus
has stolen their wits.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Drag them to ship" -> lotus_rescue_crew
@CHOICE "Leave them behind" -> lotus_abandon

@ROOM lotus_rescue_crew
@DESC
You haul the weeping men
to the ships by force and
bind them to the benches.
They curse you now but
will thank you later.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET crew_dragged
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Set sail at once" -> cyclops_island

@ROOM lotus_abandon
@DESC
You leave them swaying
among the blossoms. Three
good men, lost to a flower.
The remaining crew rows
in grim silence. Guilt
gnaws at your heart.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET crew_abandoned
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Set sail" -> cyclops_island

@ROOM lotus_rescue
@DESC
You push the blossoms
aside and order all men
back aboard. None tasted
the cursed fruit. Wise
Odysseus, cunning even in
small things.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Set sail" -> cyclops_island

@ROOM cyclops_island
@DESC
A green island of wild
goats and high cliffs. You
spy a vast cave mouth on
the hillside. Smoke rises
from within. Sheep bleat
in enormous pens.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Enter the cave" -> cyclops_cave
@CHOICE "Stay by the ships" -> aeolus_island

@ROOM cyclops_cave
@DESC
Inside, wheels of cheese
line the walls. The cave
is vast. Then a shadow
darkens the entrance. A
one-eyed giant rolls a
boulder across the door.
Polyphemus the Cyclops
has trapped you.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Say you are Nobody" -> cyclops_nobody
@CHOICE "Give your true name" -> cyclops_named

@ROOM cyclops_nobody
@DESC
"I am Nobody," you say.
That night, you sharpen an
olive stake in the fire.
While he sleeps, you drive
it into his eye. He howls.
"Nobody is hurting me!"
The other giants ignore
his cries. No help comes.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET nobody_trick
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Escape under sheep" -> cyclops_escape

@ROOM cyclops_named
@DESC
"I am Odysseus, sacker of
Troy!" you boast. You
blind him with the stake
but as you flee, he prays:
"Father Poseidon, avenge
me upon Odysseus!"
The sea itself becomes
your enemy.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET poseidon_curse
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Escape under sheep" -> cyclops_escape

@ROOM cyclops_escape
@DESC
You cling to the belly of
a great ram as it ambles
past the blinded giant.
His groping hands feel
only wool. One by one your
men slip free. You run
for the black ships.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Sail away" -> aeolus_island

@ROOM aeolus_island
@DESC
The floating isle of King
Aeolus, master of winds.
He feasts you for a month,
then gives you a gift: a
leather bag containing all
contrary winds. Only the
west wind blows free to
carry you home.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Guard the bag" -> wind_guard
@CHOICE "Trust crew with it" -> wind_crisis

@ROOM wind_guard
@DESC
Nine days you clutch the
bag, sleepless. On the
tenth, Ithaca appears on
the horizon! But then
exhaustion claims you.
Your crew, thinking it
holds gold, opens the bag.
All winds burst free.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Watch Ithaca vanish" -> circe_approach

@ROOM wind_crisis
@DESC
Your crew opens the bag on
the second night, sure it
holds treasure. All winds
shriek free at once. The
storm drives you far from
any course you knew.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Endure the tempest" -> circe_approach

@ROOM circe_approach
@DESC
Weeks later, a green isle
appears. Smoke rises from
a stone palace hidden
among ancient oaks. Your
men are starving. You must
explore.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Search the shore" -> circe_herb
@CHOICE "Go to the palace" -> circe_palace

@ROOM circe_herb
@DESC
Among the rocks you find a
strange white flower with
a black root. A divine
scent rises from it. Some
god has placed it here
for you.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM moly_herb "Moly Herb" "White flower, black root. Proof against enchantment."
@CHOICE "Go to the palace" -> circe_palace
@CHOICE "Smell it closely" -> circe_herb

@ROOM circe_palace
@DESC
The sorceress Circe stands
in her doorway, radiant
and terrible. She offers a
golden cup of wine. Your
men have already drunk.
They root in the pigpen,
transformed to swine.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Drink the wine" -> circe_doom
@CHOICE "Show the moly herb" -> circe_ally @NEED moly_herb
@CHOICE "Draw your sword" -> circe_sword

@ROOM circe_doom
@DESC
The wine is sweet. Your
limbs twist and shorten.
Coarse bristles erupt from
your skin. You try to
scream but only a squeal
emerges.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You are a pig now. You should have found protection."

@ROOM circe_sword
@DESC
You leap at her with drawn
blade. She is impressed by
your daring. "No mortal
has resisted me before."
She restores your men and
swears an oath of aid.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET circe_friend
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Ask about home" -> circe_counsel

@ROOM circe_ally
@DESC
You eat the moly and drink
without fear. The magic
fails. Circe gasps. "You
must be Odysseus! Only he
could resist my art." She
frees your men at once.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET circe_friend
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Ask about home" -> circe_counsel @USE moly_herb

@ROOM circe_counsel
@DESC
Circe speaks gravely: "You
must descend to the land
of the dead and consult
the prophet Tiresias. Only
he can guide you home."
She draws you a map.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM circe_map "Circe's Map" "A map to the Underworld and back again."
@CHOICE "Sail for the dead" -> underworld_shore

@ROOM underworld_shore
@DESC
At the world's edge, you
beach your ship. The River
of Ocean flows here into
shadow. You dig a trench
and pour offerings of milk
and dark blood. Ghosts
crowd forward, gibbering.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Summon Tiresias" -> tiresias @NEED circe_map
@CHOICE "Flee this place" -> sirens_approach

@ROOM tiresias
@DESC
The blind prophet drinks
the blood and his dead
eyes focus. "Hear me,
Odysseus. You will reach
the island of the Sun god.
His golden cattle graze
there. DO NOT EAT THEM.
If you do, all is lost."
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET tiresias_warning
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Return to daylight" -> underworld_exit @USE circe_map

@ROOM underworld_exit
@DESC
You climb from the trench
of blood and shadows. The
sun strikes your face like
a blessing. Your crew
weeps with relief to see
you return from death.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Sail onward" -> sirens_approach

@ROOM sirens_approach
@DESC
Haunting song drifts over
the water. Ahead, a rocky
isle gleams white with the
bones of sailors. The
Sirens sing of glory and
knowledge. Your men grip
the oars, entranced.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Plug ears with wax" -> sirens_safe
@CHOICE "Listen to the song" -> sirens_doom

@ROOM sirens_doom
@DESC
The song is everything you
ever desired. You order
the helmsman to steer for
the rocks. He obeys,
smiling. The hull shatters
on the reef of bones.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The Sirens' song was your last. Use wax next time."

@ROOM sirens_safe
@DESC
Beeswax seals every ear.
You alone hear the Sirens,
lashed to the mast as you
ordered. Their song is
unbearable beauty. You
scream to be freed. But
your men row on, deaf,
and the song fades.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET sirens_passed
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Sail the strait" -> scylla_strait

@ROOM scylla_strait
@DESC
The passage narrows. On
the left cliff, six long
necks sway: Scylla, each
head fanged. On the right,
Charybdis the whirlpool
swallows the sea itself.
There is no safe path.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Hug Scylla's cliff" -> scylla_pass
@CHOICE "Risk the whirlpool" -> charybdis_doom
@CHOICE "Try the middle" -> middle_pass

@ROOM charybdis_doom
@DESC
The whirlpool yawns wide.
Your ship tilts, slides,
and is swallowed whole.
Down into the black gullet
of the sea. Nothing
surfaces.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Charybdis devours all. Scylla takes only six."

@ROOM scylla_pass
@DESC
Six heads strike like
serpents. Six men scream
and are gone, snatched to
the cliffs above. You hear
them call your name as
they die. The price of
passage is paid in blood.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET scylla_loss
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Sail on, grieving" -> sun_island

@ROOM middle_pass
@DESC
Both monsters attack. The
whirlpool drags your stern
while Scylla takes men
from the bow. You lose
twelve men and half your
oars before breaking free.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET heavy_losses
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Limp onward" -> sun_island

@ROOM sun_island
@DESC
Storms trap you on this
isle for a month. Golden
cattle graze the meadows,
magnificent and sacred.
Your crew grows skeletal
with hunger.
@IF tiresias_warning
Tiresias said: do not eat
the cattle of the Sun!
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Forbid the cattle" -> sun_patience @NEED tiresias_warning
@CHOICE "Let crew eat" -> sun_wrath
@CHOICE "Hunt for fish" -> sun_forage

@ROOM sun_patience
@DESC
You hold firm, though your
men weep with hunger. On
the fortieth day, the
storm breaks. A warm wind
rises. The golden cattle
watch as you depart,
unharmed and blessed.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Sail on" -> calypso_island

@ROOM sun_wrath
@DESC
Your starving crew kills
the cattle while you
sleep. The meat sizzles
but the hides crawl and
the flesh lows on the
spit. Zeus sees all. A
thunderbolt splits your
ship. Only you survive,
clinging to wreckage.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET crew_destroyed
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Drift on the waves" -> calypso_island

@ROOM sun_forage
@DESC
You set hooks and lines
and scour the shore for
roots and shellfish. It is
barely enough. When the
storm lifts, you sail with
hollow cheeks but clear
conscience.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Sail on" -> calypso_island

@ROOM calypso_island
@DESC
A paradise isle. The nymph
Calypso takes you in. She
offers immortality, youth
eternal, and her love
forever. Seven years pass
in her embrace. But in the
night you weep, staring
across the sea toward home.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Stay with Calypso" -> calypso_doom
@CHOICE "Beg to leave" -> calypso_raft

@ROOM calypso_doom
@DESC
You choose paradise. The
centuries pass like honey.
Penelope dies waiting.
Telemachus never knows his
father. Ithaca forgets
the name of Odysseus.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Immortality without home is just a beautiful prison."

@ROOM calypso_raft
@DESC
Calypso weeps but relents.
She helps you fell great
trees and build a raft.
She fills it with wine and
bread and water. "Go then,
mortal. Seek your death
and your glory."
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Sail for Ithaca" -> ithaca_shore

@ROOM ithaca_shore
@DESC
Twenty years since you
left. The rocky shore of
Ithaca at last. But smoke
rises from your palace.
Over a hundred suitors
feast on your wealth and
court your wife. You are
one man against many.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Disguise as beggar" -> ithaca_palace
@CHOICE "Storm the palace" -> ithaca_fight

@ROOM ithaca_palace
@DESC
In rags, you enter your
own hall. The suitors mock
the old beggar. They hurl
bread and bones. But
Penelope appears: she will
marry whoever can string
the great bow of Odysseus.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET disguised
@CHOICE "String the bow" -> bow_strung

@ROOM ithaca_fight
@DESC
You charge through the
gate with a roar. A hundred
swords turn toward you.
But grey-eyed Athena walks
beside you. Terror strikes
the suitors. They fall
like wheat before the
scythe.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Seek Penelope" -> victory

@ROOM bow_strung
@DESC
The suitors try and fail,
one after another. Then
the old beggar asks for a
turn. They laugh. You take
the great bow, string it
in one smooth motion, and
send an arrow through
twelve axe-heads.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Reveal yourself" -> victory

@ROOM victory
@DESC
@IF crew_destroyed
You stand alone. Every
companion is dead. But you
are home.
@ENDIF
@IF heavy_losses
Few survived the voyage.
But those who did will sing
of it forever.
@ENDIF
@IF poseidon_curse
Poseidon's wrath follows
you still. One last quest
awaits, inland, carrying
an oar until a stranger
calls it a winnowing fan.
@ENDIF
@IF !crew_destroyed
Your loyal crew kneels
before their king,
returned at last.
@ENDIF
Penelope tests you with
the secret of your bed,
carved from a living olive
tree. You answer true.
She weeps. You weep. Twenty
years end in an embrace.
@ENDDESC
@WIN "Odysseus reclaims his throne. The long journey ends. Score: {score}"
